{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When a soul sins.</b> It does not write here 'when a man sins' but rather 'a soul,' and likewise ״הנפש החוטאת היא תמות״ — to teach that the essence of sin depends on the soul. Parable: two men sinned against a king, one a foreigner and one of his palace servants. They brought both up to the platform for judgment, and the king ordered the foreigner released and the palace servant punished with afflictions. His palace servants said to him: but this one too sinned against you! He said to them: this one is a foreigner and does not recognize my goodness, but this one, who is of my household and recognizes my goodness yet rebelled against me — this punishment is deserved. Thus the body is a foreigner, created from below, but the soul, which is from above, whose obligation is to be pure yet sinned nonetheless — therefore the body is cast into the grave and the soul receives the afflictions. And in the time to come the Holy One, blessed be He, brings body and soul and judges them, etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:50.624065445Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}